{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbFvhHXPvat9ADUv8ZBi", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Both lists and tuples are ordered sequences that can hold any mix of types. The main difference is that **lists are mutable and tuples are immutable**.\n\n| | List | Tuple |\n|---|---|---|\n| Syntax | `[1, 2, 3]` | `(1, 2, 3)` or `1, 2, 3` |\n| Mutable? | Yes. You can append, remove or reassign items. | No. It's fixed once created. |\n| Hashable? | No | Yes, if all its elements are hashable |\n| Usable as a dict key or set member? | No | Yes |\n| Methods | Many (`append`, `extend`, `insert`, `pop`, `remove`, `sort`, `reverse`, \u2026) | Only `count` and `index` |\n| Memory and speed | Somewhat larger, with extra space reserved for growth | Smaller and slightly faster to create |\n\n```python\nnums = [1, 2, 3]\nnums[0] = 10        # fine\nnums.append(4)      # fine\n\npoint = (1, 2)\npoint[0] = 10       # TypeError: 'tuple' object does not support item assignment\n\nlocations = {(40.7, -74.0): \"NYC\"}   # tuple as dict key: OK\nlocations = {[40.7, -74.0]: \"NYC\"}   # TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'\n```\n\n**How people usually choose:**\n- Use a **list** for a variable-length collection of similar items that may change, like a list of users or lines from a file.\n- Use a **tuple** for a fixed-size record where each position has its own meaning, like `(x, y)`, `(name, age)` or several return values from a function. Also use one when you need something hashable or want to signal that the data shouldn't change.\n\n**Gotchas:**\n- A one-element tuple needs a trailing comma: `(5,)` is a tuple, but `(5)` is just the integer `5`.\n- A tuple's immutability is shallow. `t = ([1, 2], 3)` can't have its items reassigned, but `t[0].append(3)` still works because the list inside it is mutable. A tuple like this also isn't hashable.\n- If you want tuples with named fields, use `collections.namedtuple` or `typing.NamedTuple`, so you can write `p.x` instead of `p[0]`."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 6676, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11903, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 6676}, "output_tokens": 7, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "1e52361a-b82b-4a5c-927a-f4a6b57e7f2a", "uuid": "355f58c2-7752-4712-909e-5c0d6406d3fa", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T09:11:28.195Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbFvguiNUm84JHfKVka8"}
